    "updated_at": "2026-11-07T20:59:20Z",
    "body": "progress: `fb71ba7` (local). The lathe fixtures now use bar-sized cylinder stock; no NC golden changed. Form, groove and thread tools are judged at their tip, and only Turning and Bore inserts get the nose disc, because a form tool's nose_radius is its crown radius. Fail-without-fix is shown: on origin/main the wider-bar pin fails with `the approach into the bar went unnamed: []`. Still open: 3 `turning_bore` tests. The law reads a bore as solid, so no boring op can post. I decided to fix it here rather than file it separately: material becomes an annulus [r_in, r_out] per station, and an axial drill ahead is credited for this law. A pin checks that a boring approach into a solid bar with no pilot is still convicted.",
